# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Railway upload filter — THIS FILE MUST LIVE AT THE GIT ROOT.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  `railway up` does not upload the directory you run it from. It walks up to
#  the git root and uploads from there, which means a `.railwayignore` sitting
#  next to the service (indexer/.railwayignore) is never read — it just gets
#  archived along with everything else. That cost us three 413s from Cloudflare
#  at ~250MB before the upload root was identified: the giveaway was that
#  emptying indexer/ made the payload BIGGER, because the stashed node_modules
#  had been moved to the repo root where nothing excluded it.
#
#  The service builds with rootDirectory=/indexer, so nothing outside indexer/
#  is needed to build or run the indexer. Everything heavy is dropped here.
#
#  EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN BELOW IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, AND THAT IS
#  LOAD-BEARING. These are gitignore semantics: an unanchored `src` matches a
#  directory named `src` at ANY depth, so it silently took `indexer/src` with
#  it. The build still succeeded — package.json and the ABIs were present, npm
#  install ran fine — and the container then crash-looped on
#
#      Event selector 'Swap' is used in a filter but does not have a
#      corresponding indexing function
#
#  which reads like a ponder.config.ts bug and is really "index.ts was never
#  uploaded, so no indexing functions were registered at all". A leading slash
#  anchors the pattern to this file's directory (the git root) only.
#
#  `node_modules` is deliberately left unanchored: we want it gone at any depth.

# Dependencies — Railway installs these itself during the Nixpacks build.
node_modules/

# Frontend: sources, static media and build output. The indexer serves an API
# and never reads any of it. These three are the bulk of the archive (~300MB).
/src/
/public/
/dist/

# Foundry: lib/ (submodules), out/ (artifacts) and cache/ are rebuilt on demand
# and are ~180MB. The indexer reads ABIs from indexer/abis, not from here.
/contracts/

# Audit sources, PDFs and the archived previous frontend.
/audit/
/archive/

# Local Ponder sync state + codegen: rebuilt on deploy, and the sync cache is
# specific to whatever database it was built against. Unanchored on purpose —
# these are junk wherever they appear.
.ponder/
generated/

# Secrets — Railway holds the real values as service variables. contracts/.env
# has held a plaintext deploy key; it must never reach a build log.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Noise.
/.git/
*.log
.DS_Store
/.vercel/
